## Custom vm.args for Glorbo — generated by Mix Release, consumed by Burrito.
##
## Burrito's erlang_launcher.zig bypasses bin/<release> and invokes erlexec
## directly with `-args_file releases/<vsn>/vm.args` (see
## deps/burrito/src/erlang_launcher.zig ~L55-73). `rel/env.sh.eex` is dead
## code under Burrito — node-distribution flags MUST live here.
##
## The `-setcookie` value is sourced from the `RELEASE_COOKIE` env var
## (honoured by Burrito at erlang_launcher.zig ~L44). `glorbo up` exports
## it from `Glorbo.Config.erl_cookie/1` when spawning the daemon.
##
## Node name pinned to loopback only — single-Director trust model
## (threat T-05-04). Distribution listener bound to an ephemeral port to
## avoid colliding with other local BEAM nodes.

## WR-09: long-name distribution. -sname wants an UNQUALIFIED short
## name and appends the host automatically; -sname glorbo@127.0.0.1
## would either be rejected outright or produce a node named
## glorbo@127.0.0.1@<hostname>. Console.help_text/0 shows
## `iex --name console@127.0.0.1 --remsh glorbo@127.0.0.1`, which
## requires -name here to match name-class (short vs long) with the
## caller. Verify manually after rebuild with:
##   glorbo up
##   iex --name console@127.0.0.1 --cookie <cookie> --remsh glorbo@127.0.0.1
-name glorbo@127.0.0.1
-kernel inet_dist_listen_min 0
-kernel inet_dist_listen_max 0
